body:
Will the global `customElements` also get a `cloneSubtree()` method and will this also support built-ins? Essentially, I'm looking for a consistent way to clone templates/fragments with different scopes. So, I'd like to be able to do something like this:

```ts
function cloneInScope(src: DocumentFragment, scope: Document | ShadowRoot | Element = document) {
  const registry = scope.customElements ?? globalThis.customElements;
  return registry.cloneSubtree(src);
}
```

Assuming the above, then at first glance, this proposal looks like it will enable all my scenarios.

```webidl
partial interface Element {
  readonly attribute CustomElementRegistry? customElements;
};
```

Why `?`? Can it return the `document.customElements` if the slot is empty?

@tpluscode you're right, but in https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/pull/865 it was decided to not pursue inheritance for now. I don't think the current design precludes it from adding it later, based on adoption and patterns established in the wild.

@justinfagnani I had some time to think about your WHATNOT feedback how `node.customElements.create()` might be seen as the new element-creation API. I think that's fair and as https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/150 is very much an unsolved problem we should probably not try to tackle it here. So instead of
```webidl
interface CustomElementRegistry {
  [CEReactions, NewObject] HTMLElement createElement(DOMString name);
  [CEReactions, NewObject] Node cloneSubtree(Node root);
};
```
I'm now thinking
```webidl
partial interface Document {
  [CEReactions, NewObject] Node cloneSubtree(Node node, CloneSubtreeOptions options);
};

dictionary CloneSubtreeOptions {
  CustomElementRegistry customElements;  
};

dictionary ElementCreationOptions { // used by Document.prototype.createElement and Document.prototype.createElementNS
  CustomElementRegistry customElements;
};
```
is the way to go. (We could also possibly overload `importNode()`, but I think there the API improvement is obvious enough that we can just make it immediately.)

The only thing that seems weird to me here is the `selfOnly` option for `importNode`. I understand the opinion that `importNode`'s default is wrong, but addressing this only via the options object seems like it might be confusing. I would suggest just adding another API to address that issue.

```js
const imported = document.importNode(element) 
console.assert(imported.childNodes.length, 0);
const importedScoped = document.importNode(element, {customElements}); 
// can fail
console.assert(importedScoped.childNodes.length, 0);
```

Can someone point me, to a comprehensive example of how the actual API **now** is to be used? I have read through the [mentioned spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html), but there is no information, or at least so to say in layman's terms on how to actually achieve, something so trivial as:

```html
<scope-v1>
  <ui-button>I am a scoped V1 Button</ui-button>
</scope-v1>
<scope-v2>
  <ui-button>I am a scoped V2 Button</ui-button>
</scope-v2>
```

I tried to figure out the API by reading the [WebKit commit](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/40e520dd495b1232d62fc0342fbc409b3649426d) but there are things that are very unclear to me. The [old proposal](https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/Scoped-Custom-Element-Registries.md), that is 5 years old hints, that simply adding a _customElement_ to a _shadowRoot_ of the element, that _"hosts"_ the _scoped registry_ should _suffice_, making sure, that this customElement has been defined to the _scoped registry_ before. This is more or less, what the [demo does](https://github.com/webcomponents/polyfills/blob/master/packages/scoped-custom-element-registry/demo/index.html).

However I am out of luck, getting this to work and any help would be greatly appreciated. I have created a very basic [example repo](https://github.com/ChristianUlbrich/scoped-element-registry-demos/), this is the [actual code](https://github.com/ChristianUlbrich/scoped-element-registry-demos/blob/main/examples/simple-demo/index.html#L27):

```js
class UiButton extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
        super();
        this.attachShadow({mode: 'open'});
    }

    connectedCallback() {
        this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `<slot>UiButtonAnyone?</slot`;
    }
}

const scopedRegistryV1 = new CustomElementRegistry();

class ScopeV1 extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
        super();
        this.attachShadow({
            mode: 'open',
            customElements: scopedRegistryV1,
        });
    }

    connectedCallback() {
        const scopedV1Button = document.createElement('ui-button', {
            customElements: scopedRegistryV1,
        });
        this.shadowRoot.appendChild(scopedV1Button);
    }
}

scopedRegistryV1.define('ui-button', UiButton);
customElements.define('scope-v1', ScopeV1);

```
What am I missing? (Of course I am running it in Safari Tech Preview 220 with Scoped custom element registry) enabled.

**Background:** I have been [presenting versioned web components](https://www.youtube.com/live/De4n7vjEO1o?t=18000s) at WebEngingeHackfest and got the feedback to have a look at the updated scoped element registries proposal / spec. I'd gladly do, but documentation seems to be _sparse_...
